     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. That is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. At that dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nSome possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1000 mg twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day, a common target dose.\n- **1700 mg/day total.** This might be 850 mg twice daily.\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1700 mg three times daily is what you meant, please confirm. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
